{"base_rate":0.22601839684625494,"brier":0.11900144546649147,"bss":0.3197354986773009,"bss_hi":0.4197959300464007,"bss_lo":0.216971183494941,"chart":{"base":[257.4,157.9],"fp":[278.1,182.7],"lead":"62,235.9 272,203.5 482,161.3 692,101.1","note":{"base":"skill 0.32 — higher than 60% of cities","fp":"low end +4pp, high end +21pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.3 °C — better than 32% of cities","rel":"promised 2% → rained 5%; promised 88% → rained 67%"},"rel":"71.6,442.3 276.2,341.8 615.5,175.2"},"country":"RO","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.07557161629434951,"ess":427.24976984983044,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Galati</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Galati rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (97%), believe about\n<b>80%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>3%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 761 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-30. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nGALATI, 7.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.32, ranked 86 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(46&ndash;142) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>326</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>5%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>129</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>20%</td><td class='num'><b>20%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'><b>36%</b></td><td class='num'>84</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>77%</td><td class='num'><b>53%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>97%</td><td class='num'><b>80%</b></td><td class='num'>83</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Galati</b> <span class=\"muted\">Romania</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;23% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 23% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.32</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>46&ndash;142\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>761 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Galati &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Galati\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 77.01720930232558,348.13953488372096 129.98000000000002,276.4927536231884 218.1007142857143,178.33333333333334 329.36628571428565,64.80000000000001 402.44626506024093,18.0 402.44626506024093,44.31325301204822 329.36628571428565,137.60000000000002 218.1007142857143,256.3333333333333 129.98000000000002,339.7971014492754 77.01720930232558,376.3565891472868 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"299.7293035479632\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"299.7293035479632\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,371.9509202453988 77.01720930232558,336.85271317829455 129.98000000000002,308.1449275362319 218.1007142857143,252.0 329.36628571428565,189.6 402.44626506024093,92.5542168674699\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 3% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 326 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"371.9509202453988\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 5%&amp;#10;It rained 12% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 129 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"77.01720930232558\" cy=\"336.85271317829455\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 20%&amp;#10;It rained 20% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"129.98000000000002\" cy=\"308.1449275362319\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 45%&amp;#10;It rained 36% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 84 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"218.1007142857143\" cy=\"252.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 77%&amp;#10;It rained 53% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"329.36628571428565\" cy=\"189.6\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 97%&amp;#10;It rained 80% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 83 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"402.44626506024093\" cy=\"92.5542168674699\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(23%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Galati the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.45) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.15).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>14%</td><td class='num'>0.155</td><td class='num'>5.5%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>217</td><td class='num'>24%</td><td class='num'>0.180</td><td class='num'>9.9%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>26%</td><td class='num'>0.407</td><td class='num'>7.0%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>27%</td><td class='num'>0.451</td><td class='num'>6.7%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":45.43687,"lon":28.05028,"n":761,"n_cities":216,"name":"Galati","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":326,"obs":0.027607361963190184,"sig":true},{"hi":0.13,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.05372093023255814,"n":129,"obs":0.12403100775193798,"sig":true},{"hi":0.35,"lo":0.13,"mean":0.20333333333333334,"n":69,"obs":0.2028985507246377,"sig":false},{"hi":0.6,"lo":0.35,"mean":0.4522619047619048,"n":84,"obs":0.35714285714285715,"sig":false},{"hi":0.9,"lo":0.6,"mean":0.7665714285714283,"n":70,"obs":0.5285714285714286,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.9,"mean":0.973012048192771,"n":83,"obs":0.7951807228915663,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":7.4,"provisional":false,"rank":86,"rank_hi":142.02499999999998,"rank_lo":45.975,"reliability":0.010822684962115258,"resolution":0.06432553760389059,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"galati","station":"GALATI","timezone":"Europe/Bucharest"}